libdatachannel v0.24.5: leave the libjuice callback before DTLS startup

MPL-2.0, like src/impl/peerconnection.cpp above. Modification history
(NereusSDR): 2026-10-05, J.J. Boyd (KG4VCF), AI-assisted via OpenAI Codex.

The poll callback holds the libjuice registry lock. Inline DTLS startup
can wait for the SSL lock while a receive worker holds SSL and sends a
relayed DTLS record through that registry. Queue startup on the existing
peer processor, preserving inline ICE state ordering and owning the peer
and exact ICE instance. Skip pending work on a closed/failed/disconnected
or replaced transport. Existing admitted-start/close overlap and post-start
cleanup remain; this is not a zero-transient-start-after-close guarantee.
No credential, fingerprint, MTU, deadline or TURN-lifetime policy changes.

--- a/src/impl/peerconnection.cpp
+++ b/src/impl/peerconnection.cpp
@@ -169,10 +169,29 @@
 						    changeIceState(IceState::Checking);
 						    changeState(State::Connecting);
 						    break;
-					    case IceTransport::State::Connected:
+					    case IceTransport::State::Connected: {
 						    changeIceState(IceState::Connected);
-						    initDtlsTransport();
+						    // Do not enter DTLS while libjuice holds its registry lock.
+						    // A receive worker can hold the SSL lock and send via ICE.
+						    auto ice = getIceTransport();
+						    mProcessor.enqueue([self = locked, ice]() {
+							    const auto peerState = self->state.load();
+							    if (self->closing.load() || peerState == State::Closed ||
+							        peerState == State::Failed || peerState == State::Disconnected ||
+							        !ice || self->getIceTransport() != ice) {
+								    return;
+							    }
+							    const auto iceState = ice->state();
+							    if (iceState != IceTransport::State::Connected &&
+							        iceState != IceTransport::State::Completed) {
+								    return;
+							    }
+							    // Close may overlap an admitted start. emplaceTransport
+							    // stops and clears it when closing is observed after start.
+							    self->initDtlsTransport();
+						    });
 						    break;
+					    }
 					    case IceTransport::State::Completed:
 						    changeIceState(IceState::Completed);
 						    break;
